  "problems": "Mango has no standalone size-guide page (shop.mango.com/gb/en/help/size-guide is a 404); charts are the per-product 'Measurements' panels, read on the Ireland store (the GB store shows the same panel in inches only by default). Product size buttons are labelled with UK numbers (4-18); the panel's equivalents table maps them to Europe 32-46, which is used as the label for jeans/trousers. The flared jeans and the wool suit trousers showed identical charts. Bottoms charts give waist and hip only, no inseam. Letter tops (t-shirt) give bust and waist only, no hip, and no EU-number equivalent (the equivalents table repeats letters). The dress chart is labelled by UK size with letter/US equivalents from that product's table; it covers only UK 6-14 on that product. Note the dress chart's waist for UK 10 / M is 72 cm while the bottoms chart's EU 38 / UK 10 is 70 cm; the charts differ and are kept separate. Charts are per product and may vary across products."
